@title Order events: three calls
@subtitle One settled, one open, one deferred
@author Platform team
@date 2026-11-12

Three decisions on the order-events platform, as they stand today.

## Queue

decision queue "Which queue carries order events?" status=settled by=2026-12-01
queue: option sqs "SQS" | managed, 14-day retention | chosen
queue: option kafka "Kafka" | replay, ops cost | rejected
queue: option sns "SNS with a fan-out topic per consumer group" | no replay, so it cannot serve the audit job | rejected
queue: question "Do we need replay beyond 14 days?" | answered: no
queue: question "Who pays for the cross-account traffic?"
queue: role decides "Ana Ruiz"
queue: role consulted "Platform team"
queue: role informed "Support"

## Region

The replica must sit near the customers who read it most.

decision region "Where does the replica run?" by=2026-11-30
region: option eu "eu-west-1" | lowest latency for EU readers
region: option us "us-east-2" | already holds the data plane and the budget
region: question "Does the contract allow EU data in us-east-2?"
region: role decides "Priya Natarajan-Wetherspoon-Hargreaves"

## Pager vendor

decision vendor "Which vendor do we pick for paging?" status=deferred by=Q1
vendor: option a "Vendor A" | cheaper per seat
vendor: option b "Vendor B" | better on-call experience
vendor: question "Does legal need to review the data terms?" | yes, by January
vendor: role decides "Head of Operations"
